<title>USA: FTC probing Seagram unit pricing practice.</title>
<headline>FTC probing Seagram unit pricing practice.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Federal Trade Commission has advised Seagram Co Ltd's Universal Music and Video Distributing it is conducting a preliminary investigation into pricing practices, Seagram said Thursday.</p>
<p>In a quarterly filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, Seagram said the FTC notified it by letter dated April 11 that the probe is to determine whether &quot;minimum advertised pricing programs used by major record distributors consitute an unfair method of competition.&quot;</p>
<p>The FTC has not made any allegations of unlawful conduct against the company, Seagram said in the filing.</p>
<p>The FTC said it cannot confirm or deny the investigation.</p>
</text>
